# Packed camera I/O

A D800 wakes its rear LCD for every gphoto2 process. One setting per process looks like a flicker and makes a shot slow.

- Read status with one `gphoto2 --get-config` list, then parse by widget label. Do not fall back to one process per key.
- Write settings with one `gphoto2` command and several `--set-config` arguments (`dual.config_args` / `dual._set_one`). Do not call `_set_widgets` or loop `--set-config` per key.
- If a widget is missing (D800 has no `isoauto`), drop that name, remember it, and send the rest once. Do not retry the whole set one key at a time.
- Do not open a second session to verify a write, sync the clock, or pulse autofocus on the shutter path unless the caller asked for that.
- GPIO release already drops USB around the 10-pin pulse. Do not add more gphoto2 calls on that path.

```python
# Bad: two processes, LCD wakes twice
gp(["--set-config", "iso=400"], port=port)
gp(["--set-config", "shutterspeed=1/125"], port=port)

# Good: one process
gp(["--set-config", "iso=400", "--set-config", "shutterspeed=1/125"], port=port)
```
